  "description": "that should cost way more\nthan it does. It's an against-the-clock bike, an aerodynamic timetrial\nor triathlon rocketship, not a modified road bike. Every spec reflects\nthat focus.\n\nYou can read those specs, look at the photo and see what it is. You can't\nsee that the frame's main triangle is now made from X-Fusion Alpha tubing,\nso the bike is much lighter and its ride more compliant.\n\nThe low-profile 650 wheels, 20-spoke front, 24 in back, are now made with\nAmerican Classic hubs, stainless spokes with alloy nipples, Ritchey deep-section\nrims and Vittoria UltraSpeed triathlon tires.\n\nThe Shimano 105 parts are enhanced with an FSA crankset with 42 and 55-tooth\nrings. Last year's fork was aluminum, now it's an aero carbon model. The\nbars and are Syntace this year, the bar ends Syntace C2 Clip Ultralite.\nThe bars and stems are size-specific; Bigger frames get wider bars and\nlonger stems. The shifters are still the best, expensive Shimano Dura-Ace\n9-speed.\nIf the road bike you've been riding just feels SLOW, but you'd rather\nspend your savings on travel to events than on a high-budget triathlon\nbike, here's the way to go. Anywhere you want to go. Fast. Aloha.",
